0:{"buildId":"IcCCyDbmxORjXmKwz37hw","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"className":"section blog-post","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Data Without Ownership Is Just Noise\",\"description\":\"Why most data initiatives stall — and how treating data as a product with a real owner changes the outcome.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-08-29\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Janio Martinez Bachmann\",\"url\":\"https://portfolio-website-two-hazel-81.vercel.app\"},\"url\":\"https://portfolio-website-two-hazel-81.vercel.app/blog/data-without-ownership-is-just-noise\"}"}}],["$","header",null,{"className":"blog-post-header","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"blog-back","children":"← All posts"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-card-meta","children":[["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-08-29","children":"August 29, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"2 min read"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Data Without Ownership Is Just Noise"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-card-tags","children":[["$","span","data products",{"className":"post-tag","children":"data products"}],["$","span","product ownership",{"className":"post-tag","children":"product ownership"}]]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Every company I have worked with — from central banks to tech giants — has more data than it knows what to do with. Dashboards multiply, pipelines hum along, and yet the same question keeps surfacing in leadership meetings: ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"Why can't we get a straight answer out of our data?\""}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The answer is rarely technical. It is almost always a question of ownership."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"data-as-a-product-not-a-byproduct","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#data-as-a-product-not-a-byproduct","className":"prose-anchor","children":"Data as a product, not a byproduct"}]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Most organizations treat data as exhaust — something that accumulates as a side effect of running the business. Reports get built on request, pipelines get patched when they break, and nobody is accountable for whether any of it actually drives a decision."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["A data ",["$","em",null,{"children":"product"}]," is different. It has:"]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"An owner"}]," who is accountable for its adoption, not just its uptime"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Users"}]," whose problems it demonstrably solves"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"A roadmap"}]," that evolves with the business, not with the backlog"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"A definition of done"}]," that includes trust — documented, tested, and understood"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"When a dataset has an owner, \"is this number right?\" has an answer and a name attached to it. When it doesn't, every consumer builds their own version of the truth, and the organization pays for the same answer five times."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"what-ownership-looks-like-in-practice","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#what-ownership-looks-like-in-practice","className":"prose-anchor","children":"What ownership looks like in practice"}]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Ownership is not a job title — it is a set of behaviors:"}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Saying no."}]," A product owner curates. Not every request deserves a dashboard; most deserve a conversation about the decision behind the request."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Measuring adoption, not delivery."}]," Shipping a data model is the start. If nobody changes a decision because of it, it failed — no matter how elegant the pipeline."]}],"\n","$L3","\n"]}],"\n","$L4","\n","$L5","\n","$L6"]}]]}],["$L7"],"$L8"]}],"isPartial":"$@9","staleTime":"$a","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Lb","isPartial":"$@c","staleTime":"$a","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Ld","isPartial":"$@e","staleTime":"$a","varyParams":"$f"},{"rsc":"$L10","isPartial":"$@11","staleTime":"$a","varyParams":"$f"},{"rsc":"$L12","isPartial":"$@13","staleTime":"$a","varyParams":null}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@14","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@15"}
